# Sole description language (HARD — copy law)

**Owner letters 2026-08-02 and 2026-08-08** — said three times: *"quit saying fully enclosed heel - dont make shit up"* · *"quit fucking saying fully enclosed this is not how we describe it."*

**Why:** this is how the brand describes its own product. Drifting invents product claims Andrew has not approved.

## Banned — never write these

fully enclosed · fully-enclosed · fully enclosed heel · fully enclosed feel · "sleek, fully enclosed feel" · enclosed heel · **any construction calling the Closed Sole *enclosed***

## Say instead — the only sanctioned wording (P-003)

- **Closed Sole:** "Heel and foot fully covered."
- **Open Sole:** "Heel exposed, mid-foot breathing hole. More grounded, barefoot feel. Natural toe splay."
- **Both:** "Both perform identically — same grip, same stability."
- **Choosing:** "Choice is preference and feel only."

```
✅ "Closed Sole is heel and foot fully covered. Both perform identically — same grip, same stability."
❌ "Closed Sole is fully enclosed."
❌ "Sleek, fully enclosed feel."
```

## No discipline split — retired 2026-08-02 (P-003)

**Never** write "Open = barre/yoga, Closed = reformer/Lagree/Megaformer" or any variant that assigns a discipline to a sole. **Both soles perform identically across all disciplines.** Also dead: recommending first-timers toward either sole (P-004 superseded).

```
✅ "Same grip, same stability, same studio uses. Choice is preference and feel only."
❌ "Closed Sole: ideal for reformer and Megaformer. Open Sole: preferred for barre and yoga."
❌ "Best for reformer footwork, barre, and Lagree" (as a Closed-Sole-only claim)
```

## Scope (all of it)

All customer-facing copy: PDP / collection / page templates in `shopify-build/templates/**` · section Liquid **and their schema defaults** in `shopify-build/sections/**` · mocks in `docs/` · `planning/`, `specs/`, `manychat-kb/` · email · ads · ManyChat KB · SEO/GEO/FAQ blocks.

**`docs/09-PRODUCT-KNOWLEDGE.md` and `manychat-kb/02-open-vs-closed-sole.md` are the SOURCE documents every agent copies from** — they must never carry banned phrasing. Retired wording stays there only under an explicit RETIRED banner, never as reusable source copy.

## Exceptions

- `backups/**`, `archive/**`, `planning/archive/**` are frozen snapshots — do not edit.
- Dated RETIRED / evidence banners recording the old wording as history are allowed. Never reuse them as source copy.

